WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:15.000
Can a tenant lose possession before a jury hears the eviction case?

00:15.000 --> 00:40.000
This rehearsal follows four kinds of authority: Indiana's Constitution,
court rules, the Indiana Code, and published opinions.

00:40.000 --> 01:10.000
The Code distinguishes preliminary possession from the final decision.
A meaningful opportunity to defend still matters.

01:10.000 --> 01:40.000
Bishop explains the preliminary-stage jury distinction.
Morton reverses for an insufficient opportunity to defend.

01:40.000 --> 02:00.000
Read the underlying opinion. A disposition label can be misleading.
Source access is not a guarantee that the legal conclusion is correct.

02:00.000 --> 02:15.000
Scripted rehearsal with live public-source retrieval; no live Muse answer.
Unofficial copies. Verify official sources. Not legal advice or a citator.
